+
+The three primary working-range measures all pass: sentence mean, ≥40-word share, and words per scene. The accepted secondary ranges also pass: ≤5-word share, paragraph median, and FK grade. This is not a failed formula movement.
+
+The meaningful drift is distributional. A 13.2-word mean alongside a 9-word median, 31.3% very short sentences, and an SD of only 11.67 produces a clipped center even though the ≥40-word tail is present. FRE 90.8 confirms that the prose reads much easier than the selected 72.3 reference. The Reader Standard benefits from the clarity, but the adult genre texture sometimes loses syntactic weight, especially in procedural explanation and repeated “He did / He did not” sequences. Repair should be selective and manual: join only adjacent short statements that are one thought, and preserve short dialogue, fight impacts, protected wording, and the road's counted rhythm.
+
+### Formula items not mechanically supplied
+
+- **Progression vocabulary density:** **UNMEASURED.** No project-specific lexicon count was supplied, so no numeric rate is invented. Qualitatively, this middle-third movement surfaces system language at a genuine turning point—the Anchor encounter, notice, cascade, and inventory—which fits the book plan's post-front-loading shape. Full-book front-loading cannot be confirmed from this movement alone.
+- **POV word share:** **UNMEASURED.** No segment-word counter was supplied. The identifiable secondary-viewpoint segments are Seln in chapters 28–29 and Havel at the start of chapter 30; the remainder of chapter 30 and chapters 31–34 are Cael. The movement intentionally carries the planned Seln and Havel windows, and neither becomes a coequal lead. Book-level 87/13 alignment cannot be confirmed from this partial coverage.
+- **Development cadence:** manually identified, not a regex proxy and not directly comparable to the 4.5/10k heuristic. Major Cael beats include choosing to price a reach before it exists (ch. 28), taking it open-eyed (ch. 31), recognizing that the room was never the system (ch. 32), accepting responsibility while distinguishing the doorway from intent (ch. 33), and naming/inventorying the new permanent cost (chs. 33–34). Supporting beats are distributed across Seln, Lira, Brom, Karis, Havel, Ephram, Rooke, Bracken, and Withrow, with Seln appropriately dominant for the keeper movement.
+- **Optional secondary signals:** **UNMEASURED.** No reproducible lexicons/counts were supplied for -*ly* words, reporting verbs, combat terms, fillers, or repeated phrases. No compliance claim is made for them.
+
+## Repair brief
+
+### 1. Correct the seal-number deduction
+
+- **Location:** chapter 30, cutters' issue ledger, lines 41–43 (“The two numbers were one apart” / “the number between them”).
+- **Observed issue:** the arithmetic language is self-contradictory. If the two registered numbers are consecutive, no number lies between them.
+- **Effect on the reader:** the key proof that the facilities-office seal was never issued becomes momentarily impossible, weakening trust in Havel's otherwise exact method.
+- **Proposed scope:** revise only the two-number relationship so the registered entries clearly sit on either side of the absent number, with no ledger line available for it. Recheck the three later references to the number and gap; no scene rewrite.
+- **Strength to preserve:** the three-way register check, Havel's refusal to interpret beyond evidence, and the decision that there will be no seventh sheet.
+
+### 2. Widen sentence cadence without touching successful beats
+
+- **Location:** selectively across the procedural/introspective runs in chapters 28–30 and the explanatory portions of chapter 33; leave dialogue, protected text, system notice, and the chapter 31 fight alone unless a specific read-aloud defect is found.
+- **Observed issue:** median 9 versus target 11, population SD 11.67 versus ~26, 31.3% sentences at five words or fewer, FRE 90.8 versus 72.3, and FK 3.87 versus 6.8. All coordinator working ranges pass, so this is controlled drift rather than a wholesale failure.
+- **Effect on the reader:** the thirteen-year-old gets excellent immediate clarity, but repeated clipped constructions can flatten procedural tension and make the adult genre register feel younger and more rhythmically predictable than intended.
+- **Proposed scope:** a bounded, sentence-by-sentence author pass joining adjacent short statements only where they form one thought, with a few clear compound-complex sentences allowed to carry deduction or reflection. Re-run the same metrics once; do not chase decimals or inflate vocabulary merely to lower Flesch scores.
+- **Strength to preserve:** the catechism, the cost leaf, the entire developed road fight, short impact lines, clear dialogue attribution, scene spacing, the birthday room, and every protected line.

