+## Repair brief
+
+### 1. Correct the seal-number deduction
+
+- **Location:** chapter 30, cutters' issue ledger, lines 41–43 (“The two numbers were one apart” / “the number between them”).
+- **Observed issue:** the arithmetic language is self-contradictory. If the two registered numbers are consecutive, no number lies between them.
+- **Effect on the reader:** the key proof that the facilities-office seal was never issued becomes momentarily impossible, weakening trust in Havel's otherwise exact method.
+- **Proposed scope:** revise only the two-number relationship so the registered entries clearly sit on either side of the absent number, with no ledger line available for it. Recheck the three later references to the number and gap; no scene rewrite.
+- **Strength to preserve:** the three-way register check, Havel's refusal to interpret beyond evidence, and the decision that there will be no seventh sheet.
+
+### 2. Widen sentence cadence without touching successful beats
+
+- **Location:** selectively across the procedural/introspective runs in chapters 28–30 and the explanatory portions of chapter 33; leave dialogue, protected text, system notice, and the chapter 31 fight alone unless a specific read-aloud defect is found.
+- **Observed issue:** median 9 versus target 11, population SD 11.67 versus ~26, 31.3% sentences at five words or fewer, FRE 90.8 versus 72.3, and FK 3.87 versus 6.8. All coordinator working ranges pass, so this is controlled drift rather than a wholesale failure.
+- **Effect on the reader:** the thirteen-year-old gets excellent immediate clarity, but repeated clipped constructions can flatten procedural tension and make the adult genre register feel younger and more rhythmically predictable than intended.
+- **Proposed scope:** a bounded, sentence-by-sentence author pass joining adjacent short statements only where they form one thought, with a few clear compound-complex sentences allowed to carry deduction or reflection. Re-run the same metrics once; do not chase decimals or inflate vocabulary merely to lower Flesch scores.
+- **Strength to preserve:** the catechism, the cost leaf, the entire developed road fight, short impact lines, clear dialogue attribution, scene spacing, the birthday room, and every protected line.

